{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn.*handle-(put|next)|handle-put|handle-next|Unknown|unknown|throw' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc:14:   rule each caller keeps.  An effect that throws propagates before any\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc:15:   successor exists, which gives a throwing effect the same guarantee for\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc:64:   with the raw answer retained.  An effect that throws propagates.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:43:  (throw (ex-info message data)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:179:(defn handle-put\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:183:   name their outcome, as v1's throw on a closed stream did.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:216:(defn handle-next\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:372:   path raises as an error. `handle-put` and `handle-next` throw for every\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:387:(defn- throw-terminal-resume!\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:429:          (throw-terminal-resume! entry terminal)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:526:          (let [result (handle-put state effect)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:538:          (let [result (handle-next state effect)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:554:              (fail \"Unknown effect\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
